And I was gearing up to write a "first pair of ascensions in
successive games" post...

I was playing a monk for the first time, and to my surprise, I was
doing pretty well.  I even beat Master Kaen on this first try.  I read
a scroll of earth to make a boulder fort around the upstairs, then
teleported out and hit Kaen with some projectiles until he zipped over
to the upstairs, in the middle of my fort.  I waited with bated breath
until he popped back out and slammed me hard, but I immediately took
his place in the fort, then took potshots at him with wands and
daggers until he expired.  Great success!

Although playing a lawful monk, at one point I donned a helm which
turned out to be opposite alignment.  I hadn't seen any artifacts yet,
but I had recovered the Castle's wand of wishing, so I thought "Eh,
why not?" and wished for the Master Key of Thievery, which was a great
help.

I'd read a pair of blessed genocide scrolls, one of which went to get
rid of those pesky L's.  I would have ordinarily used the other to get
rid of h's, but I hadn't encountered any magic markers, so I wiped out
mimics in the hope of getting one or more in Orcus Town.  (It didn't
work.)

I had a stressful moment when Orcus summoned Demogorgon soon after we
started fighting.  I've performed rashly in that situation in the
past, but I kept my head this time.  I zapped a wand of digging
downward, leaving Orcus behind but taking Demogorgon with me.  I
engraved Elbereth, and when Demogorgon retreated briefly to the
upstairs, I took some scrolls of teleportation out of my bag, cursed
them with my last vial of unholy water, and levelported to safety back
up on level 15.  Whew!

I was determined to be fully prepared on my next descent.  I had a
bunch of junk scrolls and potions which I blanked by jumping into the
Castle moat, and then, for the first time, I tried the strategy of
reading a blessed scroll of remove curse while confused to produce a
good supply of holy and unholy water.  I gathered my belongings and
went back up to the nearest altar to identify the beatitude of some of
my other items.  I had a bag of tricks on me, so I thought I'd get in
one last sacfest.  After a few unproductive sacrifices, the bag
produced an "h," which I casually attacked, taking it for a dwarf.

Slurp, slurp, slurp.  It was a mind flayer.

Shocked, I retreated, and it came after me.  I zapped it with a wand,
but it shrugged it off closed to melee range again.  I figured I'd
better check its hit points, so I quickly pressed "asl," as I always
move my stethoscope to the "s" slot.  Unfortunately, in my inventory-
wrangling with the remove-curse-scroll technique, items had migrated
to other slots.  I don't know what "s" item I applied, but my "l"
became a melee attack.

Slurp, slurp, slurp.  Another brain-suck attack, and I was dead.  My
monk only had about an 8 Int to start with, so that was all it took.

Augh, augh, AUGH.  If only I had slowed down and kept my head, I could
easily have teleported out of danger, or teleported the flayer away,
or dug down to the next level, or probably saved myself in any number
of other ways.

And now that I think about it, I actually got a throne genocide quite
early in the game, which I used on master mind flayers.

What rotten luck.


